Third-party notices of the artefacts
------------------------------------

Third-party components are licensed under the licences of their owners. Each
artefact that includes them carries their notices:

* The server's image, ghcr.io/flowtivo/tinfirm-server, in /licenses/, beside
  LICENSE and ee/LICENSE:
  - THIRD-PARTY-server.txt: the server's runtime dependencies and their
    licences, as license-maven-plugin lists them in the Maven build
    (server/pom.xml). Each jar keeps its own licence files.
  - THIRD-PARTY-web.txt: the web app's 3rdpartylicenses.txt (below).
* The runner host's archives, tinfirm-runner-host-<version>-<target>, beside
  LICENSE and ee/LICENSE: THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt, the full licence text of
  every crate the binary is built with, of the Rust standard library and, in
  the Linux builds, of musl libc. The file is runner/THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt,
  which cargo-about generates from runner/Cargo.lock (make runner-licences).
  The runner host's image, ghcr.io/flowtivo/tinfirm-runner-host, carries it
  as /licenses/THIRD-PARTY-runner.txt.
* The web app: its production build (npm run build in web/) writes the
  notices of the npm packages it bundles to 3rdpartylicenses.txt, beside
  browser/ in web/dist/tinfirm-web/. The server's image, which serves the web
  app, carries the file as /licenses/THIRD-PARTY-web.txt.

The Compose archive and the Helm chart carry LICENSE. The packages of the
base images carry their licences in each image's /usr/share/doc/, and the
images a deployment pulls from their vendors, such as PostgreSQL and LiteLLM,
carry their own.

Which licences a dependency may have, and how CI checks them, is decided in
docs/adr/0082-licence-notices-and-dependency-licences.md.
